<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alexander Karađorđević</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1806–1885</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Alexander Karadjordjević, Prince Alexander of Serbia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alexander Karađorđević, son of the rebel leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karadorde">Karađorđe</a>, was Prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> from 1842 to 1858. He was raised to the throne by the Constitutionalists after the Obrenović family was driven out, and his reign saw the building of a modern administration and legal code. He was deposed by the St Andrew's Day Assembly in 1858; his son became King Peter I.</p></div>
